Author: Arne Juul <arnej@vespa.ai>
Date:   Fri Sep 11 19:29:18 2026 +0000

    [CUDA] Fix sm_75 build of the FP8 block-scaled GEMV
    
    The tensor-core GEMV has two entry points over one body: a plain one and
    MatMulBlockScaledFp8MmaGemvKernelPinned, which carries
    __launch_bounds__(32 * KSplit, 3). For its only instantiation (KSplit = 16)
    that asks for 512 * 3 = 1536 resident threads per SM -- exactly what Ada
    offers, and what Fp8MmaGemvPinsResidency gates the entry point to (SM89+),
    where pinning three blocks per SM turns a 1.21-wave grid into a single wave.
    
    nvcc, however, codegens every instantiation for every architecture in
    --generate-code, not just the ones that can launch it. On Turing (sm_75,
    1024 threads/SM) 1536 is out of range and ptxas aborts, so any build whose
    architecture list includes sm_75 fails to compile the file even though the
    kernel is unreachable there at runtime.
    
    Make the min-blocks hint architecture-conditional through __CUDA_ARCH__,
    which nvcc redefines on each per-architecture device pass: 3 on SM89+, 1
    (an inert occupancy hint) below it, where the code is dead anyway. The
    alternative -- compiling the entry point away below SM89 -- does not work,
    because the host pass still needs the symbol to form the launch.
    
    Verified by emitting PTX per target: the kernel keeps .minnctapersm 3 at
    compute_89 and gets .minnctapersm 1 at compute_75, and the file now builds
    clean for 75/80/89. No change on SM89+, and no dispatch or shape selection
    is affected.
    
